(4416483, 633662, 67152, '<td valign="top">Awesome stuff!  Congrats on the Blue!  It was tough competition and this surely deserves a ribbon.</td>', 'Awesome stuff!  Congrats on the Blue!  It was tough competition and this surely deserves a ribbon.', '2008-01-23 05:53:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4416486, 631262, 67152, '<td valign="top">Karen - Congrats on the Red.  This is excellent.  The sky so soft and creamy and the building and snow so sharp and detailed.  Good stuff!</td>', 'Karen - Congrats on the Red.  This is excellent.  The sky so soft and creamy and the building and snow so sharp and detailed.  Good stuff!', '2008-01-23 05:54:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4416490, 633316, 67152, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your first (of many to come) ribbon!  This is excellent - one of my favorites in the challenge.</td>', 'Congrats on your first (of many to come) ribbon!  This is excellent - one of my favorites in the challenge.', '2008-01-23 05:55:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4416496, 633154, 68035, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on the excellent score and the great placement.  Thoroughly deserved for a picture that went way beyond the challenge requirement and showed not only a deserted building but a poigniant story as well<br/> <br/>Really like the black and white conversion, which again is all the more impressive as it was done in basic.  Lovely composition and application of the rule of thirds.  Certainly not a cheery picture but one that tells a story that is too often untold and is very cool for doing so</td>', 'Congratulations on the excellent score and the great placement.  Thoroughly deserved for a picture that went way beyond the challenge requirement and showed not only a deserted building but a poigniant story as well Really like the black and white conversion, which again is all the more impressive as it was done in basic.  Lovely composition and application of the rule of thirds.  Certainly not a cheery picture but one that tells a story that is too often untold and is very cool for doing so', '2008-01-23 05:58:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4416497, 632673, 67152, '<td valign="top">Alain - I like the high contrast treatment on this one.  The separation of the sky from the roof is too cool!</td>', 'Alain - I like the high contrast treatment on this one.  The separation of the sky from the roof is too cool!', '2008-01-23 05:58:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(4416500, 631218, 67152, '<td valign="top">What a great space!  And a darn nice photo too! I think the use of the moving person really adds something great to the image - i just wonder about the placement of the stairwell and the doorway  being slightly cropped out - but that is SOOOOOO minor!</td>', 'What a great space!  And a darn nice photo too! I think the use of the moving person really adds something great to the image - i just wonder about the placement of the stairwell and the doorway  being slightly cropped out - but that is SOOOOOO minor!', '2008-01-23 06:01:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4416502, 633083, 54878, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by FrankRobinson:</b></div><hr/><i> Can I ask (out of curiosity) why you used such a high ISO? I also have a Canon 400D and on the couple of occasions that I have been forced to ISO 1600 (indoor sports / really gloomy wedding etc) the noise has rendered the shots really hard to PP. Outside I would not have thought that it was necessary?<br/> <br/>Cheers! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>A bit of a cock up really, I''d been shooting indoors the night before and didn''t reset the ISO, probably because it was so windy up there and was beginning to rain so I was in a bit of a rush.  Luckilly it didn''t cause too much in the way of noise.<br/> <br/>It is quite heavily USM''d, I know that it''s not an effect that is to everyones taste but I quite like the the definition that it brings to the brickwork.</td>', 'Originally posted by FrankRobinson: Can I ask (out of curiosity) why you used such a high ISO? I also have a Canon 400D and on the couple of occasions that I have been forced to ISO 1600 (indoor sports / really gloomy wedding etc) the noise has rendered the shots really hard to PP. Outside I would not have thought that it was necessary? Cheers!   A bit of a cock up really, I''d been shooting indoors the night before and didn''t reset the ISO, probably because it was so windy up there and was beginning to rain so I was in a bit of a rush.  Luckilly it didn''t cause too much in the way of noise. It is quite heavily USM''d, I know that it''s not an effect that is to everyones taste but I quite like the the definition that it brings to the brickwork.', '2008-01-23 06:02:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4416504, 633154, 67152, '<td valign="top">Charlene - I love the details and distorted perspective to add to the drama of the image.  That is one harsh sky! But you did a nice job controlling it.</td>', 'Charlene - I love the details and distorted perspective to add to the drama of the image.  That is one harsh sky! But you did a nice job controlling it.', '2008-01-23 06:02:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4416510, 633204, 67152, '<td valign="top">Steve!  I love this one - very different from many of your entries and it really works.  I think this was greatly underappreciated.  I didn''t get to vote, but I would have given this at least an 8. I have always wanted to go shoot at Norwich, but I was always afraid to have the security guys show up! <br/> <br/>The composition and the way the doorways lead you into the darkness really adds to the metaphor.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Steve!  I love this one - very different from many of your entries and it really works.  I think this was greatly underappreciated.  I didn''t get to vote, but I would have given this at least an 8. I have always wanted to go shoot at Norwich, but I was always afraid to have the security guys show up!  The composition and the way the doorways lead you into the darkness really adds to the metaphor. ', '2008-01-23 06:06:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4416515, 633760, 67152, '<td valign="top">I love this one and gave it a 7 during voting.  The textures created by the broken windows and the high contrast created by the bushes, the steel wall, and the windows really gives this one some pop!  (I really can''t believe the score!!!)</td>', 'I love this one and gave it a 7 during voting.  The textures created by the broken windows and the high contrast created by the bushes, the steel wall, and the windows really gives this one some pop!  (I really can''t believe the score!!!)', '2008-01-23 06:09:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4416517, 633850, 47852, '<td valign="top">94th?  How on earth did this end up way down there?  I thought this was a unique perspective of an abandoned building... almost one of those ''beauty in the everyday'' type shots.  Great repetition, symmetry and details to look at.  I looked at this for a while trying to decide if I liked the ground at the bottom or if I would have preferred it to be out of the shot (if in fact the building was big enough to find a spot where the ground wasn''t in the foreground), but decided that it helped to give a little extra shape to the shot, instead of just a 3x3 grid.<br/> <br/>Anyway... I thought this was a great take on the challenge, and a welcome change from all the old buildings hidden in a bunch of gnarled trees.</td>', '94th?  How on earth did this end up way down there?  I thought this was a unique perspective of an abandoned building... almost one of those ''beauty in the everyday'' type shots.  Great repetition, symmetry and details to look at.  I looked at this for a while trying to decide if I liked the ground at the bottom or if I would have preferred it to be out of the shot (if in fact the building was big enough to find a spot where the ground wasn''t in the foreground), but decided that it helped to give a little extra shape to the shot, instead of just a 3x3 grid. Anyway... I thought this was a great take on the challenge, and a welcome change from all the old buildings hidden in a bunch of gnarled trees.', '2008-01-23 06:10:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4416518, 633759, 67152, '<td valign="top">Excellent image and fantastic lighting.  It really captures the feeling of abandonment.  I am not sure why this received such a low score.  I thought it was excellent</td>', 'Excellent image and fantastic lighting.  It really captures the feeling of abandonment.  I am not sure why this received such a low score.  I thought it was excellent', '2008-01-23 06:10:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4416519, 633426, 67152, '<td valign="top">My favorite from the challenge. Fabulous work using high contrast and interesting point of view.  keep it up, YOU ROCK!</td>', 'My favorite from the challenge. Fabulous work using high contrast and interesting point of view.  keep it up, YOU ROCK!', '2008-01-23 06:11:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4416522, 633316, 34462, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your first ribbon and a new personal best.</td>', 'Congrats on your first ribbon and a new personal best.', '2008-01-23 06:12:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4416523, 633785, 67152, '<td valign="top">Deb - Really nice details.  It''s too bad about the score - I really thought this was excellent and should have given you a high 5s.  I wonder if a wider crop to provide more contrast and a little more real estate on the screen would have helped you a bit...maybe next time!</td>', 'Deb - Really nice details.  It''s too bad about the score - I really thought this was excellent and should have given you a high 5s.  I wonder if a wider crop to provide more contrast and a little more real estate on the screen would have helped you a bit...maybe next time!', '2008-01-23 06:12:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4416527, 633801, 47852, '<td valign="top">Wow, 115th?  I really didn''t agree with the masses in this challenge.  Others commented on the reflections ruining the shot, but I thought they were just the thing that made this shot unique!  The leftover signs sitting in the back make you wonder what the building was used for, and the reflections give a glimpse of color, and show that life is still going on, right outside the doors of this abandoned building.  One of the few shots in the challenge that really told a story for me.  I think it was a great take on the challenge!</td>', 'Wow, 115th?  I really didn''t agree with the masses in this challenge.  Others commented on the reflections ruining the shot, but I thought they were just the thing that made this shot unique!  The leftover signs sitting in the back make you wonder what the building was used for, and the reflections give a glimpse of color, and show that life is still going on, right outside the doors of this abandoned building.  One of the few shots in the challenge that really told a story for me.  I think it was a great take on the challenge!', '2008-01-23 06:16:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4416530, 633156, 67152, '<td valign="top">Anne - Well...I loved it.  Sorry to see this one got such a low score.  The use of snow to create a feeling of abandonment and cold works really well for me.  Maybe it is a bit tight cropped for the DPC crowd.</td>', 'Anne - Well...I loved it.  Sorry to see this one got such a low score.  The use of snow to create a feeling of abandonment and cold works really well for me.  Maybe it is a bit tight cropped for the DPC crowd.', '2008-01-23 06:19:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4416533, 633562, 34462, '<td valign="top">You are right. It is like a theatre backdrop. It''s a beautiful photo. Congrats on your 6th place finish and what looks like your first top 10.</td>', 'You are right. It is like a theatre backdrop. It''s a beautiful photo. Congrats on your 6th place finish and what looks like your first top 10.', '2008-01-23 06:21:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(4416538, 633833, 67152, '<td valign="top">Nice building!  I like the  the perspective to get the overhang in while leaving some room on both sides.  I think it is a bit dark all around and may suffer from a mostly centered composition.  <br/> <br/>By being so tightly cropped, I am not sure if it really gives the feeling of abandonment as much as a more wide spaced image could do for you.  The top rated entries in the challenge seemed to create the feeling that the whole area was abandoned, not just the building.</td>', 'Nice building!  I like the  the perspective to get the overhang in while leaving some room on both sides.  I think it is a bit dark all around and may suffer from a mostly centered composition.   By being so tightly cropped, I am not sure if it really gives the feeling of abandonment as much as a more wide spaced image could do for you.  The top rated entries in the challenge seemed to create the feeling that the whole area was abandoned, not just the building.', '2008-01-23 06:23:33.000000', NULL, 0),
