(4424018, 631327, 35357, '<td valign="top">This is a tough exposure, with the bright clouds and the dark subject.  I''d suggest the Shadow/Highlight (or equivalent) tool to lighten up the building and darken the clouds.<br/>Cheers</td>', 'This is a tough exposure, with the bright clouds and the dark subject.  I''d suggest the Shadow/Highlight (or equivalent) tool to lighten up the building and darken the clouds.Cheers', '2008-01-25 10:47:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(4424122, 633645, 44877, '<td valign="top">This is a very cool photo, Jeanne! In the thumb, it looks like the silhouette of a man kneeling down and bending over - like he''s breaking and entering - and I love that door in the back. Excellent but not well appreciated, unfortunately.</td>', 'This is a very cool photo, Jeanne! In the thumb, it looks like the silhouette of a man kneeling down and bending over - like he''s breaking and entering - and I love that door in the back. Excellent but not well appreciated, unfortunately.', '2008-01-25 11:42:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4424124, 633492, 80912, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments. I''m still not sure what I did wrong, lol.<br/> <br/>As for the pulling back and/or negative space - there wasn''t really much "space." It was pretty cluttered. I originally thought of using one of these -<br/><a href="//img.photobucket.com/albums/v432/hopkind/Tests/posted05.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//img.photobucket.com/albums/v432/hopkind/Tests/th_posted05.jpg'', strrpos(''//img.photobucket.com/albums/v432/hopkind/Tests/th_posted05.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//img.photobucket.com/albums/v432/hopkind/Tests/th_posted05.jpg"/></a> <br/><a href="//img.photobucket.com/albums/v432/hopkind/Tests/posted10.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//img.photobucket.com/albums/v432/hopkind/Tests/th_posted10.jpg'', strrpos(''//img.photobucket.com/albums/v432/hopkind/Tests/th_posted10.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//img.photobucket.com/albums/v432/hopkind/Tests/th_posted10.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>I did have one from a different angle where there''s a large patch of grass in the foreground, but it doesn''t really have as much impact as it does w/ the sign. <br/> <br/><a href="//img.photobucket.com/albums/v432/hopkind/Tests/DSCF2608.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//img.photobucket.com/albums/v432/hopkind/Tests/th_DSCF2608.jpg'', strrpos(''//img.photobucket.com/albums/v432/hopkind/Tests/th_DSCF2608.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//img.photobucket.com/albums/v432/hopkind/Tests/th_DSCF2608.jpg"/></a>(This and the following images are straight from the camera - no processing, just resized by photobucket)<br/> <br/>Here''s the whole shed w/ the background -<br/><a href="//img.photobucket.com/albums/v432/hopkind/Tests/DSCF2611.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//img.photobucket.com/albums/v432/hopkind/Tests/th_DSCF2611.jpg'', strrpos(''//img.photobucket.com/albums/v432/hopkind/Tests/th_DSCF2611.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//img.photobucket.com/albums/v432/hopkind/Tests/th_DSCF2611.jpg"/></a> <br/>and the original shot I used - <a href="//img.photobucket.com/albums/v432/hopkind/Tests/DSCF2610.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//img.photobucket.com/albums/v432/hopkind/Tests/th_DSCF2610.jpg'', strrpos(''//img.photobucket.com/albums/v432/hopkind/Tests/th_DSCF2610.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//img.photobucket.com/albums/v432/hopkind/Tests/th_DSCF2610.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Thanks again<br/> <br/></td>', 'Thanks for the comments. I''m still not sure what I did wrong, lol. As for the pulling back and/or negative space - there wasn''t really much "space." It was pretty cluttered. I originally thought of using one of these -   I did have one from a different angle where there''s a large patch of grass in the foreground, but it doesn''t really have as much impact as it does w/ the sign.  (This and the following images are straight from the camera - no processing, just resized by photobucket) Here''s the whole shed w/ the background - and the original shot I used -   Thanks again ', '2008-01-25 11:42:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4424872, 633316, 7810, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your first (of many ) ribbon. I am glad you chose the sepia ... it adds to the old feel of the shot.</td>', 'Congrats on your first (of many ) ribbon. I am glad you chose the sepia ... it adds to the old feel of the shot.', '2008-01-25 15:33:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4425021, 633492, 36065, '<td valign="top">I really think that you had a good starting image.  The composition does feel a bit cramped, especially with the sign so close to the edge of the image.  Leaving some negative space can be as simple as just leaving some extra space around you main focal point, just like you did in the top two alternatives below.  I do like those much better, with the one at the top being my fav of the two.  If you could have shot this with a better, more interesting sky, I think your score would have grown some.  I also think that it would be a more interesting shot in the summer with the greenery on the vines, but we live by the hand of Langdon here.  He put the challenge in for this week, not the summertime.  Nice work with the post-processing.</td>', 'I really think that you had a good starting image.  The composition does feel a bit cramped, especially with the sign so close to the edge of the image.  Leaving some negative space can be as simple as just leaving some extra space around you main focal point, just like you did in the top two alternatives below.  I do like those much better, with the one at the top being my fav of the two.  If you could have shot this with a better, more interesting sky, I think your score would have grown some.  I also think that it would be a more interesting shot in the summer with the greenery on the vines, but we live by the hand of Langdon here.  He put the challenge in for this week, not the summertime.  Nice work with the post-processing.', '2008-01-25 17:20:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4425921, 631262, 68035, '<td valign="top">woohoo chappers!!!!!  Sorry it has taken me so long to comment on this shot but I have been working away.  Many many congratulations on the ribbon, the 7+ average and your second highest score<br/> <br/>I think it takes a hell of a photographer to produce an image of such beauty out of what is essentially an ugly subject, but you have done this remarkably<br/> <br/>Incredible tones and colours and a beuatiful haunting composition<br/> <br/>Brilliant</td>', 'woohoo chappers!!!!!  Sorry it has taken me so long to comment on this shot but I have been working away.  Many many congratulations on the ribbon, the 7+ average and your second highest score I think it takes a hell of a photographer to produce an image of such beauty out of what is essentially an ugly subject, but you have done this remarkably Incredible tones and colours and a beuatiful haunting composition Brilliant', '2008-01-26 04:38:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4425923, 631671, 68035, '<td valign="top">Peter<br/> <br/>Great image and - what is becoming customary for you - a very impressive score and finish<br/> <br/>I loved the broad range of earthtones in the shot and loved the elongated shadow of the chair.  Great sharpness as well<br/> <br/>Possibly for me the doll was a fraction of an overstatement but very cool nonetheless</td>', 'Peter Great image and - what is becoming customary for you - a very impressive score and finish I loved the broad range of earthtones in the shot and loved the elongated shadow of the chair.  Great sharpness as well Possibly for me the doll was a fraction of an overstatement but very cool nonetheless', '2008-01-26 04:42:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4425927, 631218, 68035, '<td valign="top">Sandy....You rock!!!!!<br/> <br/>Its funny I would have never associated this image with you and this makes me love it even more!!!<br/> <br/>Beautifully dark and the ''ghost'' figure really adds a whole heap of atmospheric ambience.  Wonderful composition that shows that great photographers can make the mundane seem striking<br/> <br/>Wonderful</td>', 'Sandy....You rock!!!!! Its funny I would have never associated this image with you and this makes me love it even more!!! Beautifully dark and the ''ghost'' figure really adds a whole heap of atmospheric ambience.  Wonderful composition that shows that great photographers can make the mundane seem striking Wonderful', '2008-01-26 04:44:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4425929, 632667, 68035, '<td valign="top">I really like this shot in terms of the wide variety of shapes that there are in the composition and the way they are interwoven.  Its a shame the sky is so harsh under the lead arch but I appreciate that there are some things that you just cant do anything about</td>', 'I really like this shot in terms of the wide variety of shapes that there are in the composition and the way they are interwoven.  Its a shame the sky is so harsh under the lead arch but I appreciate that there are some things that you just cant do anything about', '2008-01-26 04:48:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(4426083, 633645, 3724, '<td valign="top">Real interesting window view. How was the water?</td>', 'Real interesting window view. How was the water?', '2008-01-26 09:40:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4426176, 631218, 65234, '<td valign="top">Didn''t vote in this challenge; cool place you have there!!  Back you go for Architecture ;-)</td>', 'Didn''t vote in this challenge; cool place you have there!!  Back you go for Architecture ;-)', '2008-01-26 10:40:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4426200, 631661, 24454, '<td valign="top">Wow, Mary!  I think this is really cool!   I can''t believe they gave this a 4.6 :(   Baaaaaaaad voters!<br/> <br/>I don''t think they much liked my blurry addition to my photo either.   Guess you gotta love those non-artsy types too, huh???    (Ok, sometimes not!)<br/> <br/></td>', 'Wow, Mary!  I think this is really cool!   I can''t believe they gave this a 4.6 :(   Baaaaaaaad voters! I don''t think they much liked my blurry addition to my photo either.   Guess you gotta love those non-artsy types too, huh???    (Ok, sometimes not!) ', '2008-01-26 10:48:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4426247, 633110, 73115, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments and tips everyone. I don''t live close enough to the barn to watch for owls and it''s not on my regular daily commute.  I think I may go back and shoot from the back of the barn and take some rain pants. Everything is so wet around these parts... I wanted to get lower but didn''t want to be a muddy mess either.  :)</td>', 'Thanks for all the comments and tips everyone. I don''t live close enough to the barn to watch for owls and it''s not on my regular daily commute.  I think I may go back and shoot from the back of the barn and take some rain pants. Everything is so wet around these parts... I wanted to get lower but didn''t want to be a muddy mess either.  :)', '2008-01-26 11:07:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(4426452, 633662, 52296, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your blue. Wonderful shot!</td>', 'Congrats on your blue. Wonderful shot!', '2008-01-26 12:50:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4426461, 633644, 52296, '<td valign="top">Congrats Bragi on your top ten finish!</td>', 'Congrats Bragi on your top ten finish!', '2008-01-26 12:52:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4426469, 631262, 52296, '<td valign="top">Congrats Karen, excellent work!</td>', 'Congrats Karen, excellent work!', '2008-01-26 12:54:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4426896, 631262, 30982, '<td valign="top">I just now noticed that this was you and not one of the Iceland people!  Congrats on the ribbon!!  A beautiful old place, and glad the weather gave you what you wanted.  Excellent shot!</td>', 'I just now noticed that this was you and not one of the Iceland people!  Congrats on the ribbon!!  A beautiful old place, and glad the weather gave you what you wanted.  Excellent shot!', '2008-01-26 15:35:27.000000', NULL, 0);
